To force a text field in Adobe Animate to display columns, you can use the `textBaseline` and `textAlign` properties in conjunction with the `text` object's `width` property. However, a more robust approach would be to use a `TextField` object with a multi-line text layout. 

Here's an example of how you can achieve this:

```as3
// Create a new TextField object
var textfield:TextField = new TextField();
textfield.width = 200; // Set the width of the text field
textfield.wordWrap = true; // Enable word wrapping
textfield.multiline = true; // Enable multi-line text

// Set the text baseline and text alignment
textfield.textBaseline = "top";
textfield.textAlign = "left";

// Add the text field to the stage
addChild(textfield);

// Set the text to display in columns
var columnText:String = "Column 1\nColumn 2\nColumn 3";
textfield.text = columnText;

// Calculate the number of columns and the width of each column
var columnCount:uint = 3;
var columnWidth:Number = textfield.width / columnCount;
var textArray:Array = columnText.split("\n");

// Loop through the text array and position each line of text
for (var i:uint = 0; i < textArray.length; i++) {
    var textLine:String = textArray[i];
    var textFormat:TextFormat = new TextFormat();
    textFormat.size = 12; // Set the font size
    textFormat.color = 0x000000; // Set the font color
    textFormat.align = "left";
    textfield.setTextFormat(textFormat);
    var textMetrics:TextMetrics = textfield.getCharBoundaries(0);
    var x:Number = i % columnCount * columnWidth;
    var y:Number = Math.floor(i / columnCount) * (textfield.height / columnCount);
    textfield.x = x;
    textfield.y = y;
    textfield.text = textLine;
}
```

This code will create a text field with the specified width and display the text in the specified columns. You can adjust the `columnCount`, `columnWidth`, and other properties to customize the layout as needed.

